import Mathlib.SetTheory.Cardinal.Finite
import MathlibLattice.Order.PatternStructure.Projection
import MathlibLattice.Order.Belief.Basic
import MathlibLattice.Order.Mobius.Cumulative
import MathlibLattice.Order.Mobius.Rota

-- The library's files carry no copyright header.
set_option linter.style.header false

/-!
# The height filtration

Let `δ : G → D` be a pattern structure and `ψ k` a sequence of projections of `D` that keep more
information as `k` grows: `ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d`. At level `k` each object `g` is described by the
fixed point `ψ k (δ g)`, which gives a sequence of description languages of increasing
resolution. This file compares the levels.

The comparison holds for any two pattern structures `δ : G → D` and `δ' : G → E` on the same
objects such that every extent of `δ'` is an extent of `δ`, that is, `δ'` is coarser than `δ`.
Then the closure of a set of objects in `δ` is contained in its closure in `δ'`, and this
characterizes the situation; join gaps shrink from `δ'` to `δ`; the coarse closure is left
adjoint to the embedding of the pattern concepts of `δ'` into those of `δ` with the same extent,
a Galois insertion (`PatternConcept.giToFine`); cumulative counts of a weighting of the objects
pull back along the embedding; the Möbius functions of the two lattices are related by Rota's
Galois connection theorem; and the coarse lattice has at most as many pattern concepts as the
fine one, with equality for finite lattices exactly when the two pattern structures have the
same extents. The coarse closure also sends object concepts to object concepts, so that point
counts, and so masses, push forward along it; this needs only the weaker condition that the
order of the objects under `δ` refines their order under `δ'`
(`PatternConcept.toCoarse_comp_ofObject_iff`, `PatternConcept.pt_ofObject_eq_sum`), which the
condition on extents implies but does not characterize. The statements about the levels of the
filtration are the instances of these for two levels `k ≤ k'`.

The descriptions need not form a complete meet-semilattice. Each statement asks only that the
descriptions of the objects of every set have a meet (`PatternStructure.IsGLBDescr`) in the
pattern structures it uses, the condition of Ganter and Kuznetsov; refining the order of the
objects does not even need meets. At level `k` the condition holds when it holds for the
projected descriptions `ψ k ∘ δ` (`PatternStructure.Projection.isGLBDescr_project`), and every
complete meet-semilattice of descriptions satisfies it at every level.

Chains of projections come from increasing sequences of sublanguages of a complete lattice of
descriptions (`PatternStructure.Projection.ofSubset_le_ofSubset_succ`); the heights of
first-order terms give such a sequence for every corpus of terms. The descriptions by clauses of a
finite corpus have meets, but the descriptions by clauses do not form a complete lattice, since an
infinite set of clauses need not have a least general generalization under θ-subsumption, so
these sublanguage projections do not apply to them: a height filtration of a corpus of clauses
needs another construction.

## Main definitions

* `MathlibLattice.Height.level ψ δ k`: the pattern structure at level `k`.
* `MathlibLattice.Height.levelGI`: for `k ≤ k'`, the Galois insertion of the pattern concepts of
  level `k` into those of level `k'`.

## Main statements

* `MathlibLattice.Height.forall_isExtent_imp_iff`: every extent of `δ'` is an extent of `δ` iff
  every closure in `δ` is contained in the closure in `δ'`.
* `MathlibLattice.Height.forall_le_imp_of_forall_isExtent_imp`: refining the extents refines the
  order of the objects; `MathlibLattice.Height.exists_forall_le_imp_not_forall_isExtent_imp`: not
  conversely.
* `MathlibLattice.Height.toCoarse_ofObjects`: the coarse closure of a generated pattern concept
  is the pattern concept generated by the same objects.
* `MathlibLattice.Height.extent_sup_toFine_sdiff_subset`: join gaps shrink under refinement.
* `MathlibLattice.Height.cum_ofObject_eq`: cumulative counts pull back.
* `MathlibLattice.Height.sum_mu_toFine_eq`: Rota's theorem for a refinement.
* `MathlibLattice.Height.natCard_eq_iff`: equality of the numbers of pattern concepts.
* `MathlibLattice.Height.antitone_extentOf_descr_level`: closures decrease with the level.
* `MathlibLattice.Height.antitone_extentOf_descr_union_sdiff_level`: join gaps decrease with the
  level; `MathlibLattice.Height.exists_not_antitone_sdiff_ofObjects_level`: the join gap of the
  pattern concepts generated by two fixed sets need not.
* `MathlibLattice.Height.pt_ofObject_level_eq_sum`, `MathlibLattice.Height.cum_ofObject_level_eq`:
  masses push forward and cumulative counts pull back along the level map.
* `MathlibLattice.Height.monotone_enatCard_level`: the number of pattern concepts increases with
  the level.

## References

* B. Ganter, S. O. Kuznetsov, *Pattern structures and their projections*, 2001.
* G.-C. Rota, *On the foundations of combinatorial theory I. Theory of Möbius functions*, 1964.
-/

open Finset IncidenceAlgebra PatternStructure PatternConcept

namespace MathlibLattice.Height

variable {G D E F R 𝕜 : Type*}

/-! ### Two pattern structures, one coarser than the other -/

section Refinement

-- The hypothesis `h` (every extent of `δ'` is an extent of `δ`) is needed in each statement
-- below that does not use it to build `toFine h`: for the constant map `δ = fun _ => ∅` and
-- `δ' g = {g}` in `Set (Fin 2)`, the closure of `{0}` is `{0, 1}` in `δ` and `{0}` in `δ'`.

-- The meets of descriptions (`IsGLBDescr`) are needed for both pattern structures in
-- `forall_isExtent_imp_iff`, and so wherever closures are compared: with the infimum on `Bool`
-- that is constantly `false`, the closure of `{true}` under `id : Bool → Bool` is `Set.univ`,
-- and with the infimum that is constantly `true`, the closure of `Set.univ` under
-- `fun _ : Unit => false` is `∅`, while in both cases the extents are those of the usual
-- infimum.

section Closure

variable [Preorder D] [InfSet D] [Preorder E] [InfSet E] {δ : G → D} {δ' : G → E}
  [IsGLBDescr δ] [IsGLBDescr δ']

/-- Every extent of `δ'` is an extent of `δ` if and only if, for every set of objects `A`, the
closure `extentOf δ (descr δ A)` of `A` in `δ` is contained in the closure of `A` in `δ'`. -/
theorem forall_isExtent_imp_iff :
    (∀ A, IsExtent δ' A → IsExtent δ A) ↔
      ∀ A : Set G, extentOf δ (descr δ A) ⊆ extentOf δ' (descr δ' A) := by
  refine ⟨fun h A => ?_, fun h A hA => isExtent_iff.2
    (((h A).trans (isExtent_iff.1 hA).le).antisymm (subset_extentOf_iff_le_descr.2 le_rfl))⟩
  obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := h _ (isExtent_extentOf δ' (descr δ' A))
  rw [← hd]
  exact fun _ => le_trans (subset_extentOf_iff_le_descr.1
    (hd ▸ subset_extentOf_iff_le_descr.2 le_rfl))

/-- If every extent of `δ'` is an extent of `δ`, the closure of a set of objects in `δ` is
contained in its closure in `δ'`. -/
theorem extentOf_descr_subset (h : ∀ A, IsExtent δ' A → IsExtent δ A) (A : Set G) :
    extentOf δ (descr δ A) ⊆ extentOf δ' (descr δ' A) :=
  forall_isExtent_imp_iff.1 h A

end Closure

section Order

variable [Preorder D] [Preorder E] {δ : G → D} {δ' : G → E}

/-- Refining the extents refines the order of the objects: if every extent of `δ'` is an extent of
`δ`, then `δ g ≤ δ g'` implies `δ' g ≤ δ' g'`, since the extent of `δ' g` in `δ'` is an extent of
`δ` containing `g`. No meets of descriptions are needed. This is the hypothesis of
`PatternConcept.toCoarse_comp_ofObject_iff` and of the push-forward of point counts
`PatternConcept.pt_ofObject_eq_sum`. -/
theorem forall_le_imp_of_forall_isExtent_imp (h : ∀ A, IsExtent δ' A → IsExtent δ A) :
    ∀ g g', δ g ≤ δ g' → δ' g ≤ δ' g' := by
  intro g g' hgg'
  obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := h _ (isExtent_extentOf δ' (δ' g))
  exact (Set.ext_iff.1 hd g').1 (le_trans ((Set.ext_iff.1 hd g).2 le_rfl) hgg')

end Order

/-- The converse of `forall_le_imp_of_forall_isExtent_imp` fails: for the objects `0, 1, 2`
described by `δ g = {g}` and by `δ' = ![{0}, {0}, {1}]` in `Set (Fin 3)`, the order of the objects
under `δ` is discrete, so it refines their order under `δ'`, while `{0, 1}`, the extent of `{0}`
in `δ'`, is not an extent of `δ`. -/
theorem exists_forall_le_imp_not_forall_isExtent_imp :
    ∃ δ δ' : Fin 3 → Set (Fin 3), (∀ g g', δ g ≤ δ g' → δ' g ≤ δ' g') ∧
      ¬∀ A, IsExtent δ' A → IsExtent δ A := by
  refine ⟨fun g => {g}, ![{0}, {0}, {1}], fun g g' h => ?_, fun h => ?_⟩
  · rw [Set.singleton_subset_singleton.1 h]
  · obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := h _ (isExtent_extentOf ![{0}, {0}, {1}] {0})
    simp [Set.ext_iff, extentOf, Fin.forall_fin_succ] at hd
    tauto

section Lattice

variable [PartialOrder D] [InfSet D] [PartialOrder E] [InfSet E] {δ : G → D} {δ' : G → E}
  [IsGLBDescr δ] [IsGLBDescr δ']

/-- If every extent of `δ'` is an extent of `δ`, the closure in `δ'` of the pattern concept of
`δ` generated by a set of objects `A` is the pattern concept of `δ'` generated by `A`. -/
theorem toCoarse_ofObjects (h : ∀ A, IsExtent δ' A → IsExtent δ A) (A : Set G) :
    toCoarse δ' (ofObjects δ A) = ofObjects δ' A :=
  le_antisymm (ofObjects_le_iff.2 (extentOf_descr_subset h A)) (ofObjects_le_iff.2
    ((subset_extentOf_iff_le_descr.2 le_rfl).trans (subset_extentOf_iff_le_descr.2 le_rfl)))

/-- Closures compose: if every extent of `δ''` is an extent of `δ'`, closing a pattern concept of
any pattern structure `δ₀` first in `δ'` and then in `δ''` is closing it in `δ''`. -/
theorem toCoarse_toCoarse {D₀ : Type*} [LE D₀] [InfSet D₀] {δ₀ : G → D₀} [PartialOrder F]
    [InfSet F] {δ'' : G → F} [IsGLBDescr δ''] (h : ∀ A, IsExtent δ'' A → IsExtent δ' A)
    (c : PatternConcept δ₀) : toCoarse δ'' (toCoarse δ' c) = toCoarse δ'' c :=
  toCoarse_ofObjects h c.extent

/-- Join gaps shrink under refinement: if every extent of `δ'` is an extent of `δ`, the join gap
of two pattern concepts of `δ` with the extents of two pattern concepts `c` and `c'` of `δ'` (the
objects in the extent of their join that lie in neither extent) is contained in the join gap of
`c` and `c'`. -/
theorem extent_sup_toFine_sdiff_subset (h : ∀ A, IsExtent δ' A → IsExtent δ A)
    (c c' : PatternConcept δ') :
    (toFine h c ⊔ toFine h c').extent \ ((toFine h c).extent ∪ (toFine h c').extent) ⊆
      (c ⊔ c').extent \ (c.extent ∪ c'.extent) :=
  Set.sdiff_subset_sdiff_left
    (sup_le ((toFine h).monotone le_sup_left) ((toFine h).monotone le_sup_right))

/-- Cumulative counts pull back under refinement: if every extent of `δ'` is an extent of `δ`,
the cumulative count of a weighting `w` of the objects along the object concept map of `δ'` at
`q` is its cumulative count along the object concept map of `δ` at the pattern concept of `δ`
with the extent of `q`. -/
theorem cum_ofObject_eq [Fintype G] [AddCommMonoid R] (h : ∀ A, IsExtent δ' A → IsExtent δ A)
    (w : G → R) (q : PatternConcept δ') :
    cum (ofObject δ') w q = cum (ofObject δ) w (toFine h q) :=
  toCoarse_comp_ofObject (forall_le_imp_of_forall_isExtent_imp h) ▸
    (giToFine h).gc.cum_comp (ofObject δ) w q

-- The instance `LocallyFiniteOrder (PatternConcept δ')` here and in `sum_mu_toFine_eq` is not an
-- extra hypothesis: the order embedding `toFine h` pulls back the instance for `δ`
-- (`OrderEmbedding.locallyFiniteOrder`), and any two instances are equal (`LocallyFiniteOrder`
-- is a subsingleton). It is an argument so that the statements apply to the instance in scope.
open Classical in
/-- Rota's Galois connection theorem for a refinement (Rota 1964): if every extent of `δ'` is an
extent of `δ`, then for a pattern concept `a` of `δ` and a pattern concept `b` of `δ'`, the sum
of `μ a x` over the pattern concepts `x` of `δ` between `a` and the image of `b` whose closure in
`δ'` is `b` is `μ (toCoarse δ' a) b` if `a` is the image of its closure in `δ'` (equivalently,
the extent of `a` is an extent of `δ'`), and `0` otherwise. -/
theorem sum_mu_toCoarse_eq_ite [LocallyFiniteOrder (PatternConcept δ)]
    [LocallyFiniteOrder (PatternConcept δ')] [AddCommGroup 𝕜] [One 𝕜]
    (h : ∀ A, IsExtent δ' A → IsExtent δ A) (a : PatternConcept δ) (b : PatternConcept δ') :
    ∑ x ∈ Icc a (toFine h b) with toCoarse δ' x = b, mu 𝕜 a x =
      if toFine h (toCoarse δ' a) = a then mu 𝕜 (toCoarse δ' a) b else 0 :=
  (giToFine h).sum_mu_eq_ite a b

open Classical in
/-- The Möbius function of a coarser pattern structure from that of a finer one (Rota 1964): if
every extent of `δ'` is an extent of `δ`, then for pattern concepts `a` and `b` of `δ'`, `μ a b`
is the sum of `μ (toFine h a) x` over the pattern concepts `x` of `δ` between the images of `a`
and `b` whose closure in `δ'` is `b`. -/
theorem sum_mu_toFine_eq [LocallyFiniteOrder (PatternConcept δ)]
    [LocallyFiniteOrder (PatternConcept δ')] [AddCommGroup 𝕜] [One 𝕜]
    (h : ∀ A, IsExtent δ' A → IsExtent δ A) (a b : PatternConcept δ') :
    ∑ x ∈ Icc (toFine h a) (toFine h b) with toCoarse δ' x = b, mu 𝕜 (toFine h a) x =
      mu 𝕜 a b := by
  rw [sum_mu_toCoarse_eq_ite, toCoarse_toFine, if_pos rfl]

end Lattice

section Card

-- Meets are needed only for the finer pattern structure `δ`: with the infimum on `Bool` that is
-- constantly `true`, the object of `Unit` described by `false` has the single pattern concept
-- `(∅, true)`, while with the usual infimum it has two, with the same two extents `∅` and
-- `Set.univ`.
variable [Preorder D] [InfSet D] [LE E] [InfSet E] {δ : G → D} {δ' : G → E} [IsGLBDescr δ]

/-- If every extent of `δ'` is an extent of `δ`, then `δ'` has at most as many pattern concepts
as `δ`. -/
theorem enatCard_le (h : ∀ A, IsExtent δ' A → IsExtent δ A) :
    ENat.card (PatternConcept δ') ≤ ENat.card (PatternConcept δ) :=
  ENat.card_le_card_of_injective (toFine h).injective

-- `Finite (PatternConcept δ)` is needed: for `δ` with infinitely many pattern concepts and `δ'`
-- the constant map to `⊤`, the left side is `1` and the right side is `0`.
/-- If every extent of `δ'` is an extent of `δ` and `δ` has finitely many pattern concepts, then
`δ'` has at most as many pattern concepts as `δ`. -/
theorem natCard_le [Finite (PatternConcept δ)] (h : ∀ A, IsExtent δ' A → IsExtent δ A) :
    Nat.card (PatternConcept δ') ≤ Nat.card (PatternConcept δ) :=
  Nat.card_le_card_of_injective _ (toFine h).injective

end Card

section CardEq

variable [Preorder D] [InfSet D] [Preorder E] [InfSet E] {δ : G → D} {δ' : G → E}
  [IsGLBDescr δ] [IsGLBDescr δ']

-- `Finite (PatternConcept δ)` is needed: for `δ g = {g}ᶜ` and `δ' g = {g}` in `Set ℕ`, every
-- subset of `ℕ` is an extent of `δ`, the extents of `δ'` are `∅`, `ℕ` and the singletons, and
-- both numbers of pattern concepts are `0`. Meets for `δ'` are needed, by the example before
-- `enatCard_le` with the roles of the two infima exchanged.
/-- If every extent of `δ'` is an extent of `δ` and `δ` has finitely many pattern concepts, the
two pattern structures have the same number of pattern concepts if and only if they have the
same extents. -/
theorem natCard_eq_iff [Finite (PatternConcept δ)] (h : ∀ A, IsExtent δ' A → IsExtent δ A) :
    Nat.card (PatternConcept δ') = Nat.card (PatternConcept δ) ↔
      ∀ A, IsExtent δ A → IsExtent δ' A := by
  refine ⟨fun hc A hA => ?_, fun h' => Nat.card_congr (Equiv.ofBijective _ ⟨(toFine h).injective,
    fun c => ⟨ofIsExtent δ' c.extent (h' _ c.isExtent_extent), PatternConcept.ext rfl⟩⟩)⟩
  obtain ⟨c, hc'⟩ := ((toFine h).injective.bijective_of_nat_card_le hc.ge).2 (ofIsExtent δ A hA)
  exact (congrArg PatternConcept.extent hc').subst (motive := IsExtent δ') c.isExtent_extent

end CardEq

end Refinement

/-! ### Chains of projections -/

section Chain

variable [Preorder D] {ψ : ℕ → Projection D} {k k' : ℕ}

-- The chain condition `hψ` is needed in each statement of this section and the next ones that
-- assume it: for `δ g = {g}` in `Set (Fin 2)`, `ψ 0 = id` and `ψ k` the projection to `⊥` for
-- `k ≥ 1`, the extent `{0}` of level `0` is not an extent of level `1`.

/-- If `ψ k ∘ ψ (k + 1) = ψ k` for every `k`, then `ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d` for every `k` and `d`. -/
theorem apply_le_apply_succ_of_comp_eq (h : ∀ k, ⇑(ψ k) ∘ ⇑(ψ (k + 1)) = ⇑(ψ k)) (k : ℕ)
    (d : D) : ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d :=
  (congrFun (h k) d).symm.trans_le ((ψ k).apply_le _)

/-- If `ψ k ∘ ψ (k + 1) = ψ k` for every `k`, then `ψ k ∘ ψ k' = ψ k` whenever `k ≤ k'`. -/
theorem comp_eq_of_le (h : ∀ k, ⇑(ψ k) ∘ ⇑(ψ (k + 1)) = ⇑(ψ k)) (hk : k ≤ k') :
    ⇑(ψ k) ∘ ⇑(ψ k') = ⇑(ψ k) := by
  induction k', hk using Nat.le_induction with
  | base => exact funext (ψ k).idempotent
  | succ n _ ih => rw [← ih, Function.comp_assoc, h n]

/-- If `ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d` for every `k` and `d`, then `ψ k d ≤ ψ k' d` whenever `k ≤ k'`. -/
theorem apply_le_apply_of_le (hψ : ∀ k d, ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d) (hk : k ≤ k') (d : D) :
    ψ k d ≤ ψ k' d :=
  monotone_nat_of_le_succ (fun k => hψ k d) hk

/-- The pattern structure at level `k` of the filtration given by the projections `ψ`: each
object `g` is described by the fixed point `ψ k (δ g)`. -/
abbrev level (ψ : ℕ → Projection D) (δ : G → D) (k : ℕ) : G → (ψ k).Fixed :=
  (ψ k).project δ

/-- Extents increase with the level: if `ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d` for every `k` and `d`, every
extent of level `k` is an extent of every level `k' ≥ k`. -/
theorem isExtent_level_of_le (hψ : ∀ k d, ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d) (δ : G → D) (hk : k ≤ k') :
    ∀ A, IsExtent (level ψ δ k) A → IsExtent (level ψ δ k') A :=
  fun _ => Projection.isExtent_project_of_le (apply_le_apply_of_le hψ hk) δ

/-- The levels of the pattern structure that describes every description by itself determine
the chain condition: `ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d` for every `k` and `d` if and only if, for every `k`,
every extent of level `k` of `id : D → D` is an extent of level `k + 1`. -/
theorem forall_apply_le_iff_isExtent_level_id :
    (∀ k d, ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d) ↔
      ∀ k (A : Set D), IsExtent (level ψ id k) A → IsExtent (level ψ id (k + 1)) A := by
  refine ⟨fun hψ k => isExtent_level_of_le hψ id k.le_succ, fun h k d => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨e, he, hed⟩ := ((ψ (k + 1)).isExtent_project_iff id).1
    (h k _ (((ψ k).isExtent_project_iff id).2 ⟨ψ k d, (ψ k).idempotent d, rfl⟩))
  exact le_trans ((Set.ext_iff.1 hed e).1 le_rfl) (he.ge.trans ((ψ (k + 1)).monotone
    (le_trans ((Set.ext_iff.1 hed (ψ k d)).2 le_rfl) ((ψ k).apply_le d))))

end Chain

section ChainPartialOrder

variable [PartialOrder D] {ψ : ℕ → Projection D}

-- A partial order is needed: on the two-element preorder with `a ≤ b ≤ a`, `ψ 0 = id` and `ψ k`
-- the constant map to `a` for `k ≥ 1` satisfy `ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d`, but `ψ 0 ∘ ψ 1 ≠ ψ 0`.
/-- For projections of a partial order, `ψ k ∘ ψ (k + 1) = ψ k` for every `k` if and only if
`ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d` for every `k` and `d`. -/
theorem comp_eq_iff_apply_le :
    (∀ k, ⇑(ψ k) ∘ ⇑(ψ (k + 1)) = ⇑(ψ k)) ↔ ∀ k d, ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d :=
  forall_congr' fun _ => Projection.le_iff_comp_eq.symm.trans Projection.le_def

end ChainPartialOrder

section ChainMeet

variable [Preorder D] [InfSet D] {ψ : ℕ → Projection D} {k k' : ℕ}

-- Each statement from here on asks that the descriptions of the objects of every set have a meet
-- (`IsGLBDescr`) at the levels it uses, the condition of Ganter and Kuznetsov for the pattern
-- structures of these levels; it is needed as for two pattern structures, the case of the
-- projections `ψ k = id`. It holds at level `k` when it holds for `ψ k ∘ δ`
-- (`PatternStructure.Projection.isGLBDescr_project`), in particular in a complete
-- meet-semilattice of descriptions.

/-- Closures decrease with the level: if `ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d` for every `k` and `d`, the
closure of a set of objects at level `k` decreases with `k`. -/
theorem antitone_extentOf_descr_level (hψ : ∀ k d, ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d) (δ : G → D)
    [∀ k, IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k)] (A : Set G) :
    Antitone fun k => extentOf (level ψ δ k) (descr (level ψ δ k) A) :=
  fun _ _ hk => extentOf_descr_subset (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk) A

/-- The description of a set at level `k` lies below its description at level `k + 1`. -/
private lemma coe_descr_level_le_succ (hψ : ∀ k d, ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d) (δ : G → D)
    [∀ k, IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k)] (A : Set G) (k : ℕ) :
    ((descr (level ψ δ k) A : (ψ k).Fixed) : D) ≤
      ((descr (level ψ δ (k + 1)) A : (ψ (k + 1)).Fixed) : D) := by
  refine ((descr (level ψ δ k) A).2.ge.trans (hψ k _)).trans ?_
  show (ψ (k + 1)).toFixed _ ≤ descr (level ψ δ (k + 1)) A
  refine (le_isGLB_iff (isGLB_descr (level ψ δ (k + 1)) A)).2 ?_
  rintro _ ⟨g, hg, rfl⟩
  exact (ψ (k + 1)).monotone ((Subtype.coe_le_coe.2
    ((isGLB_descr (level ψ δ k) A).1 ⟨g, hg, rfl⟩)).trans ((ψ k).apply_le (δ g)))

/-- Descriptions increase with the level: if `ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d` for every `k` and `d`, the
description of a set of objects at level `k`, the meet of the descriptions `ψ k (δ g)` of its
objects among the fixed points of `ψ k`, increases with `k`. -/
theorem monotone_coe_descr_level (hψ : ∀ k d, ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d) (δ : G → D)
    [∀ k, IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k)] (A : Set G) :
    Monotone fun k => ((descr (level ψ δ k) A : (ψ k).Fixed) : D) :=
  monotone_nat_of_le_succ (coe_descr_level_le_succ hψ δ A)

/-- Join gaps decrease with the level: if `ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d` for every `k` and `d`, then for
sets of objects `A` and `A'`, the objects in the closure of `A ∪ A'` at level `k` that lie in
neither set form a set that decreases with `k`. When `A` and `A'` are extents at level `k`, this
set is the join gap at level `k` of the pattern concepts with extents `A` and `A'`. -/
theorem antitone_extentOf_descr_union_sdiff_level (hψ : ∀ k d, ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d)
    (δ : G → D) [∀ k, IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k)] (A A' : Set G) :
    Antitone fun k => extentOf (level ψ δ k) (descr (level ψ δ k) (A ∪ A')) \ (A ∪ A') :=
  fun _ _ hk => Set.sdiff_subset_sdiff_left (antitone_extentOf_descr_level hψ δ (A ∪ A') hk)

/-- The number of pattern concepts increases with the level: if `ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d` for every
`k` and `d`, the number of pattern concepts of level `k`, in `ℕ∞`, is monotone in `k`. -/
theorem monotone_enatCard_level (hψ : ∀ k d, ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d) (δ : G → D)
    [∀ k, IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k)] :
    Monotone fun k => ENat.card (PatternConcept (level ψ δ k)) :=
  fun _ _ hk => enatCard_le (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk)

-- Finiteness of the levels is needed: for `δ g = {g}` in `Set ℕ`, `ψ 0` the projection to `⊥`
-- and `ψ k = id` for `k ≥ 1`, level `0` has one pattern concept and level `1` infinitely many.
/-- If `ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d` for every `k` and `d` and every level has finitely many pattern
concepts, the number of pattern concepts of level `k` is monotone in `k`. -/
theorem monotone_natCard_level (hψ : ∀ k d, ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d) (δ : G → D)
    [∀ k, IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k)] [∀ k, Finite (PatternConcept (level ψ δ k))] :
    Monotone fun k => Nat.card (PatternConcept (level ψ δ k)) :=
  fun _ _ hk => natCard_le (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk)

-- Finiteness of level `k'` is needed: for `δ g = {g}ᶜ` in `Set ℕ`, `ψ 0` the projection whose
-- fixed points are `∅`, `ℕ` and the complements of singletons, and `ψ k = id` for `k ≥ 1`, both
-- levels are infinite, but `{0, 1}` is an extent of level `1` only.
/-- If `ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d` for every `k` and `d`, `k ≤ k'` and level `k'` has finitely many
pattern concepts, levels `k` and `k'` have the same number of pattern concepts if and only if
they have the same extents. -/
theorem natCard_level_eq_iff (hψ : ∀ k d, ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d) {δ : G → D}
    [IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k)] [IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k')] (hk : k ≤ k')
    [Finite (PatternConcept (level ψ δ k'))] :
    Nat.card (PatternConcept (level ψ δ k)) = Nat.card (PatternConcept (level ψ δ k')) ↔
      ∀ A, IsExtent (level ψ δ k') A → IsExtent (level ψ δ k) A :=
  natCard_eq_iff (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk)

end ChainMeet

section ChainLattice

variable [PartialOrder D] [InfSet D] {ψ : ℕ → Projection D} {k k' : ℕ}

/-- The pattern concept generated by `A ∪ A'` is the join of those generated by `A` and `A'`. -/
private lemma ofObjects_union {δ : G → D} [IsGLBDescr δ] (A A' : Set G) :
    ofObjects δ (A ∪ A') = ofObjects δ A ⊔ ofObjects δ A' :=
  GaloisConnection.l_sup (u := PatternConcept.extent) fun _ _ => ofObjects_le_iff

/-- The join gap of the pattern concepts generated by two sets of objects need not decrease with
the level, since the closures of the two sets also shrink. A witness: the objects `0, 1, 2` of
`Fin 3` described by the attribute sets `{0, 2}`, `{1}` and `{0}`, the projection `ψ 0` keeping
the attributes `0` and `1` and `ψ k = id` for `k ≥ 1`, and the sets `{0}` and `{1}`, whose join
gap is `∅` at level `0` and `{2}` at level `1`. -/
theorem exists_not_antitone_sdiff_ofObjects_level :
    ∃ (ψ : ℕ → Projection (Set (Fin 3))) (δ : Fin 3 → Set (Fin 3)) (A A' : Set (Fin 3)),
      (∀ k d, ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d) ∧
        ¬Antitone fun k => (ofObjects (level ψ δ k) A ⊔ ofObjects (level ψ δ k) A').extent \
          ((ofObjects (level ψ δ k) A).extent ∪ (ofObjects (level ψ δ k) A').extent) := by
  refine ⟨fun k => ⟨⟨fun d => d ∩ if k = 0 then {0, 1} else Set.univ,
    fun _ _ h => Set.inter_subset_inter_left _ h⟩, fun _ => Set.inter_subset_left,
    fun _ => Set.inter_eq_left.2 Set.inter_subset_right⟩, ![{0, 2}, {1}, {0}], {0}, {1},
    fun k d => Set.inter_subset_inter_right _ (by simp), fun h => ?_⟩
  simp only [← ofObjects_union] at h
  refine (h (Nat.zero_le 1) (?_ : (2 : Fin 3) ∈ _)).2 (Or.inl ?_)
  all_goals
    simp only [ofObjects, ofIsIntent, mem_extentOf, Set.mem_sdiff, Set.mem_union,
      ← Subtype.coe_le_coe, descr, Projection.coe_sInf_fixed, Set.image_image, level,
      Projection.project, Function.comp_apply, Projection.coe_toFixed]
    dsimp only [DFunLike.coe]
    simp

/-- Join gaps decrease with the level: if `ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d` for every `k` and `d` and
`k ≤ k'`, the join gap at level `k'` of the images of two pattern concepts of level `k` is
contained in their join gap at level `k`. -/
theorem extent_sup_toFine_level_sdiff_subset (hψ : ∀ k d, ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d) {δ : G → D}
    [IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k)] [IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k')] (hk : k ≤ k')
    (c c' : PatternConcept (level ψ δ k)) :
    (toFine (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk) c ⊔ toFine (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk) c').extent \
        ((toFine (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk) c).extent ∪
          (toFine (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk) c').extent) ⊆
      (c ⊔ c').extent \ (c.extent ∪ c'.extent) :=
  extent_sup_toFine_sdiff_subset _ c c'

/-- The level map is a Galois insertion: if `ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d` for every `k` and `d` and
`k ≤ k'`, the closure at level `k` of the pattern concepts of level `k'` is left adjoint to the
embedding of the pattern concepts of level `k` into those of level `k'` with the same extent,
and closing an embedded pattern concept gives it back. -/
def levelGI (hψ : ∀ k d, ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d) (δ : G → D) [IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k)]
    [IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k')] (hk : k ≤ k') :
    GaloisInsertion (toCoarse (level ψ δ k) : PatternConcept (level ψ δ k') → _)
      (toFine (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk)) :=
  giToFine _

/-- The level map sends object concepts to object concepts: if `ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d` for every
`k` and `d` and `k ≤ k'`, the closure at level `k` of the object concept of `g` at level `k'` is
the object concept of `g` at level `k`. -/
theorem toCoarse_level_ofObject (hψ : ∀ k d, ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d) {δ : G → D}
    [IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k)] [IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k')] (hk : k ≤ k') (g : G) :
    toCoarse (level ψ δ k) (ofObject (level ψ δ k') g) = ofObject (level ψ δ k) g :=
  toCoarse_ofObject (forall_le_imp_of_forall_isExtent_imp (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk)) g

/-- The level maps compose: if `ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d` for every `k` and `d` and `k ≤ k'`, closing a
pattern concept of any level first at level `k'` and then at level `k` is closing it at
level `k`. -/
theorem toCoarse_level_toCoarse_level (hψ : ∀ k d, ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d) {δ : G → D} {k'' : ℕ}
    [IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k)] [IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k')] (hk : k ≤ k')
    (c : PatternConcept (level ψ δ k'')) :
    toCoarse (level ψ δ k) (toCoarse (level ψ δ k') c) = toCoarse (level ψ δ k) c :=
  toCoarse_toCoarse (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk) c

open Classical in
/-- Masses push forward along the level map: if `ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d` for every `k` and `d` and
`k ≤ k'`, the point count of a weighting of the objects along the object concept map of level
`k` at `q` is the sum of its point counts along the object concept map of level `k'` at the
pattern concepts whose closure at level `k` is `q`. -/
theorem pt_ofObject_level_eq_sum [Fintype G] [AddCommMonoid R]
    (hψ : ∀ k d, ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d) {δ : G → D} [IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k)]
    [IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k')] (hk : k ≤ k') [Fintype (PatternConcept (level ψ δ k'))]
    (w : G → R) (q : PatternConcept (level ψ δ k)) :
    pt (ofObject (level ψ δ k)) w q =
      ∑ p with toCoarse (level ψ δ k) p = q, pt (ofObject (level ψ δ k')) w p :=
  pt_ofObject_eq_sum (forall_le_imp_of_forall_isExtent_imp (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk)) w q

/-- Cumulative counts pull back along the level map: if `ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d` for every `k` and
`d` and `k ≤ k'`, the cumulative count of a weighting of the objects along the object concept
map of level `k` at `q` is its cumulative count along the object concept map of level `k'` at the
pattern concept with the extent of `q`. -/
theorem cum_ofObject_level_eq [Fintype G] [AddCommMonoid R] (hψ : ∀ k d, ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d)
    {δ : G → D} [IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k)] [IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k')] (hk : k ≤ k')
    (w : G → R) (q : PatternConcept (level ψ δ k)) :
    cum (ofObject (level ψ δ k)) w q =
      cum (ofObject (level ψ δ k')) w (toFine (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk) q) :=
  cum_ofObject_eq (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk) w q

-- The instance for level `k` here and in `sum_mu_toFine_level_eq` is not an extra hypothesis: it
-- is pulled back from the instance for level `k'` along `toFine (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk)`,
-- as in `sum_mu_toCoarse_eq_ite`.
open Classical in
/-- Rota's theorem for two levels (Rota 1964): if `ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d` for every `k` and `d`
and `k ≤ k'`, then for a pattern concept `a` of level `k'` and a pattern concept `b` of level `k`,
the sum of `μ a x` over the pattern concepts `x` of level `k'` between `a` and the image of `b`
whose closure at level `k` is `b` is `μ (toCoarse (level ψ δ k) a) b` if `a` is the image of its
closure at level `k` (equivalently, the extent of `a` is an extent of level `k`), and `0`
otherwise. -/
theorem sum_mu_level_eq_ite (hψ : ∀ k d, ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d) {δ : G → D}
    [IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k)] [IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k')] (hk : k ≤ k')
    [LocallyFiniteOrder (PatternConcept (level ψ δ k))]
    [LocallyFiniteOrder (PatternConcept (level ψ δ k'))] [AddCommGroup 𝕜] [One 𝕜]
    (a : PatternConcept (level ψ δ k')) (b : PatternConcept (level ψ δ k)) :
    ∑ x ∈ Icc a (toFine (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk) b) with toCoarse (level ψ δ k) x = b,
        mu 𝕜 a x =
      if toFine (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk) (toCoarse (level ψ δ k) a) = a then
        mu 𝕜 (toCoarse (level ψ δ k) a) b else 0 :=
  sum_mu_toCoarse_eq_ite (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk) a b

open Classical in
/-- The Möbius function of a level from that of a finer level (Rota 1964): if
`ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d` for every `k` and `d` and `k ≤ k'`, then for pattern concepts `a` and `b`
of level `k`, `μ a b` is the sum, over the pattern concepts `x` of level `k'` between the images
of `a` and `b` whose closure at level `k` is `b`, of the Möbius function of level `k'` at the
image of `a` and `x`. -/
theorem sum_mu_toFine_level_eq (hψ : ∀ k d, ψ k d ≤ ψ (k + 1) d) {δ : G → D}
    [IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k)] [IsGLBDescr (level ψ δ k')] (hk : k ≤ k')
    [LocallyFiniteOrder (PatternConcept (level ψ δ k))]
    [LocallyFiniteOrder (PatternConcept (level ψ δ k'))] [AddCommGroup 𝕜] [One 𝕜]
    (a b : PatternConcept (level ψ δ k)) :
    ∑ x ∈ Icc (toFine (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk) a) (toFine (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk) b)
        with toCoarse (level ψ δ k) x = b, mu 𝕜 (toFine (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk) a) x =
      mu 𝕜 a b :=
  sum_mu_toFine_eq (isExtent_level_of_le hψ δ hk) a b

end ChainLattice

end MathlibLattice.Height
